text:
The moon, all white and round, came up tonight

 To bathe her beauty in light;

 I stood on my hill to see it go down--

Here is what I wrote, but not sure how much he would approve;

"You who know me now, yet never met me before,
With all my flaws you loved me and for that I love you more."

And I, whose life is one with hers,
Have never known how to love her better;

The woman who shares my joys and pains:

Who gives me part of herself to share ;

In those days
there were no roads on our islands,
and so all who sailed had to walk or ride horses;

My life is like this, full of toil and pains;
I do not have time to rest or ease;
But I will be patient — all things come at last!
